\import{macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}

\taxon{Definition}
\title{Policy stamp and provenance}
\tag{ftip}
\tag{provenance}

\p{A \strong{policy stamp} #{\nu} identifies the policy that generated an
action. It contains a checkpoint identifier, a parameterization identifier,
and the accepted-update index. A rollout generated throughout by one policy
has a behaviour stamp #{\nu_b}.}

\p{Section 3 of \citef{schulman2017proximal} distinguishes the current policy
from the behaviour policy. The reuse analysis of \citef{miao2026when} requires
the same distinction. The policy stamp is an FTIP proposal motivated by both
sources. The parameterization identifier records changes such as
an adapter merge or a tokenizer revision that a weight hash alone may miss.}

\p{A stamp identifies provenance; it is not an estimate of policy distance.
Likelihood ratios and age are computed later for a particular update attempt.}
